# The pack's own merge lane, on the hub only (pack sd:9668). Its lane runs
# review, `make check` and a merge, 30-60 minutes. Inside the shared
# lane-run job it kept that run alive, and launchd starts no tick of a job
# while a run lives, so every other lane waited up to 120 minutes.
#
# Install it in `<config>/cron-jobs/jobs/<hub>/` only once the pack has
# pack sd:9668 (`sd-ship lane run --help` lists `--skip`), beside a copy of
# lane-run.job whose command line reads, escaped as below:
#
#   JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}/bin/sd-ship\" lane run --hosted --skip \"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}\""
#
# so the shared run leaves this lane alone. A held runner lock makes a slot
# exit at once, so the two jobs never run one lane twice. A plain `lane run`
# refuses on a machine that does not host the lane, so a moved pack lane
# stops here; move this job with it. Bulkmove holds no lock for it: that
# stage runs only on a satellite and skips one holding the hub role.
#
# SD_PACK_ROOT is escaped so the `bash -c` that runs the command reads it,
# after ~/.config/shell/env.sh; this file is sourced before env.sh is.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/5 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="120m"
JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}/bin/sd-ship\" -C \"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}\" lane run"
